eturns fallback metadata; call lease_account to receive the next credential.\n\nAs an orchestrator, work the inbox: get_inbox lists what waits (blocked, in review,\nawaiting approval) with decision and artifact ids; list_decisions(view=\"detail\") or\nget_decision reads the questions (get_inbox(view=\"actionable\") gives, per row,\nwho may answer, what each answer does, what it holds up and labelled evidence: hints\nonly, nothing is executed); list_artifacts, verify_artifact and read_artifact\ncheck evidence; answer_decision or answer_decisions acts (give each answer a\nrequest_id, so retries are safe); get_tasks(ids) reads the effects back. edit_task changes a task's title, spec,\nacceptance, priority, capabilities, pins or dependencies (pass its `version`). Lists\nare paged: `total` counts every match, follow `next_cursor` while `has_more`. If a\ntool you need is missing, say which and stop; do not script REST around it.\n\nFor the fleet: inspect_pool shows what each instance is proven to run (a fact's\n`source`, or `unknown`); recycle_instance and drain_agent never interrupt claimed\nwork (recycle_instance(requeue=true) and release_task requeue it without costing an\nattempt); admins change options with update_pool(expected_version=the pool's version).\nget_agent_hygiene reports lost/gone aggregates and alerts; archive_agents (admin)\narchives old lost/gone identities in bounded batches. wait_for_events(subject_type,\nsubject_id) waits for the change to happen instead of polling; then inspect_pool or\nget_tasks reads back the effect. steer_task sends an instruction to the worker\nholding a claimed task; it arrives on that worker's next heartbeat.\n\nOrchestrators: read the skill at skill://argus-orchestrator/SKILL.md (also the\nprompt \"argus-orchestrator\") before acting: what you must and must not do.\"\"\"\n\nserver = MCPServer(\"argus\", version=\"0.1.0\", instructions=INSTRUCTIONS)\n\n# The orchestrator skill, in the Agent Skills format (SKILL.md), served as an MCP\n# resource and as a prompt so any connected client can load it (MCP operations 3.4).\nORCHESTRATOR_SKILL = (\n    Path(__file__).parent / \"skills\" / \"argus-orchestrator\" / \"SKILL.md\"\n).read_text()\nserver.add_resource(\n    TextResource(\n        uri=\"skill://argus-orchestrator/SKILL.md\",\n        name=\"argus-orchestrator\",\n        title=\"Argus orchestrator skill\",\n        description=\"What an orchestrator can and must do with the Argus tools.\",\n        mime_type=\"text/markdown\",\n        text=ORCHESTRATOR_SKILL,\n    )\n)\n\n\n@server.prompt(\n    name=\"argus-orchestrator\",\n    title=\"Argus orchestrator\",\n    description=\"Load the Argus orchestrator skill before running the fleet.\",\n)\ndef orchestrator_skill() -> str:\n    return ORCHESTRATOR_SKILL\n\n\n_app: FastAPI | None = None\n\n# Who a tool is listed to (MCP operations 3.4). Listing is not access control:\n# every call is still decided by the REST endpoint it forwards to.\nAGENTS = frozenset({Scope.WORKER, Scope.ORCHESTRATOR})\nMANAGERS = frozenset({Scope.ORCHESTRATOR, Scope.ADMIN})\nADMINS = frozenset({Scope.ADMIN})\nANYONE = frozenset(Scope)\naudiences: dict[str, frozenset[Scope]] = {}\n\n\ndef tool[F: FunctionType](audience: frozenset[Scope]) -> Callable[[F], F]:\n    def register(fn: F) -> F:\n        audiences[fn.__name__] = audience\n        return server.tool()(fn)\n\n    return register\n\n\nasync def _list_tools_for_caller(\n    ctx: ServerRequestContext[Any, Any], call_next: CallNext\n) -> HandlerResult:\n    \"\"\"Answer `tools/list` with only the tools the caller's scope can use.\"\"\"\n    result = await call_next(ctx)\n    # The SDK hands middleware the serialized result; tests pin that shape.\n    if ctx.method != \"tools/list\" or not isinstance(result, dict):\n        return result\n    headers = getattr(ctx.request, \"headers\", None) or {}\n    scheme, _, token = headers.get(\"authorization\", \"\").partition(\" \")\n    assert _app is not None\n    try:\n        if scheme.lower() != \"bearer\" or not token:\n            raise UnauthorizedError(\"missing bearer token\")","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01QooW3h3apwezsssnyv6KE6","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
