cs/specs/task-edit.spec.md\",\"\"\"- No change to creation, retry, cancel, approval, archive or PR management.\n\"\"\",\"\"\"- No change to creation, retry, cancel, approval, archive or PR management.\n  To assemble a definition before anything can claim it, draft and publish it\n  instead ([task drafts](task-drafts.spec.md)); editing a published task follows\n  this spec.\n\"\"\")\nsub(\"docs/specs/task-dependencies.spec.md\",\"\"\"- Removing a `cancelled` or `failed` dependency is how a stranded task is\n  released (gap 3): no other mechanism is added.\n\"\"\",\"\"\"- Removing a `cancelled` or `failed` dependency is how a stranded task is\n  released (gap 3): no other mechanism is added.\n- Tasks that depend on each other and do not exist yet are drafted and\n  published together ([task drafts](task-drafts.spec.md) 3.3): references between\n  drafts become edges to the real new task ids, with the same existence, cycle\n  and 100-dependency rules, in the publishing transaction.\n\"\"\")\nsub(\"docs/specs/mcp-operations.spec.md\",\"\"\"| Edit a task | `PATCH /tasks/{id}` | `edit_task` | covered by [task edit](task-edit.spec.md): same fields, version precondition and errors |\n\"\"\",\"\"\"| Edit a task | `PATCH /tasks/{id}` | `edit_task` | covered by [task edit](task-edit.spec.md): same fields, version precondition and errors |\n| Draft and publish tasks | `/task-drafts`, `POST /task-drafts/publish` | `create_task_draft` … `publish_task_drafts` | covered by [task drafts](task-drafts.spec.md): versioned drafts, idempotent publish, `atomic` or `partial` on both surfaces |\n\"\"\")\nEOF\ngrep -n \"^## 3.4\" -A30 docs/specs/mcp-operations.spec.md | head -40"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4863,"cache_read_input_tokens":103991,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":4863},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"