{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01YM7MyRuaueKRiZtc46wQLx","type":"tool_result","content":"544:## 3.4 Discovery\n545-\n546-- One mount at `/mcp`. A server middleware (`MCPServer.middleware`, the SDK's\n547-  documented hook) resolves the bearer token's scope and filters the\n548-  `tools/list` result. A missing or invalid token gets a `401 unauthorized`\n549-  error. The SDK passes the middleware a serialized result, and tests pin that.\n550-  If an SDK upgrade breaks the hook, the fallback is a second mount at\n551-  `/mcp/ops`.\n552-- Each tool declares its audience: agents (worker and orchestrator tokens),\n553-  managers (orchestrator and admin), or anyone. Workers see the task-working\n554-  and knowledge tools. Orchestrators see everything. Admins see everything\n555-  except the tools that need an agent identity (`claim_task`, `heartbeat`, …).\n556-  Admin-only tools (`update_pool`, `set_model_policy`, `reset_model_policy`) appear only for admins. A test calls every\n557-  listed tool for each scope and fails if REST refuses one on scope. Calling an\n558-  unlisted tool still follows REST's rules. Hiding a tool is not access control.\n559-- The server `instructions` name the inbox journey and the fleet journey. They\n560-  also give the fallback when a tool is missing: say which tool is missing and\n561-  stop; do not script REST around it. The same text goes to\n562-  `integrations/nanoclaw/README.md` for orchestrator setup.\n563-- **Orchestrator skill.** The orchestrator's playbook (what it can, must and\n564-  must not do with these tools) is one file in the open Agent Skills format,\n565-  `apps/api/src/argus_api/skills/argus-orchestrator/SKILL.md`, linked from\n566-  `skills/argus-orchestrator/` at the repo root for skill installers. The server\n567-  serves it, unchanged, as the resource `skill://argus-orchestrator/SKILL.md`\n568-  (`text/markdown`) and as the prompt `argus-orchestrator`, and the\n569-  `instructions` point to it. It holds no rule REST does not enforce. A test\n570-  fails if it names a tool that does not exist.\n571-\n572-## 3.5 Benchmark\n573-\n574-- `apps/api/bench/mcp_inbox.py` seeds a fixed synthetic set: 40 tasks over 3","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e60805ed-c36d-4e22-8274-acc0a44d64d1","uuid":"69f80fa9-f121-4694-8723-c1869b91a318","timestamp":"2026-10-31T23:04:11.255Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"544:## 3.4 Discovery\n545-\n546-- One mount at `/mcp`. A server middleware (`MCPServer.middleware`, the SDK's\n547-  documented hook) resolves the bearer token's scope and filters the\n548-  `tools/list` result. A missing or invalid token gets a `401 unauthorized`\n549-  error. The SDK passes the middleware a serialized result, and tests pin that.\n550-  If an SDK upgrade breaks the hook, the fallback is a second mount at\n551-  `/mcp/ops`.\n552-- Each tool declares its audience: agents (worker and orchestrator tokens),\n553-  managers (orchestrator and admin), or anyone. Workers see the task-working\n554-  and knowledge tools. Orchestrators see everything. Admins see everything\n555-  except the tools that need an agent identity (`claim_task`, `heartbeat`, …).\n556-  Admin-only tools (`update_pool`, `set_model_policy`, `reset_model_policy`) appear only for admins. A test calls every\n557-  listed tool for each scope and fails if REST refuses one on scope. Calling an\n558-  unlisted tool still follows REST's rules. Hiding a tool is not access control.\n559-- The server `instructions` name the inbox journey and the fleet journey. They\n560-  also give the fallback when a tool is missing: say which tool is missing and\n561-  stop; do not script REST around it. The same text goes to\n562-  `integrations/nanoclaw/README.md` for orchestrator setup.\n563-- **Orchestrator skill.** The orchestrator's playbook (what it can, must and\n564-  must not do with these tools) is one file in the open Agent Skills format,\n565-  `apps/api/src/argus_api/skills/argus-orchestrator/SKILL.md`, linked from\n566-  `skills/argus-orchestrator/` at the repo root for skill installers. The server\n567-  serves it, unchanged, as the resource `skill://argus-orchestrator/SKILL.md`\n568-  (`text/markdown`) and as the prompt `argus-orchestrator`, and the\n569-  `instructions` point to it. It holds no rule REST does not enforce. A test\n570-  fails if it names a tool that does not exist.\n571-\n572-## 3.5 Benchmark\n573-\n574-- `apps/api/bench/mcp_inbox.py` seeds a fixed synthetic set: 40 tasks over 3","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01YM7MyRuaueKRiZtc46wQLx","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
