{"type":"system","subtype":"compact_boundary","uuid":"4a9134ca-a11c-4094-86ee-200b2abaad99","compact_metadata":{"trigger":"auto","pre_tokens":132404,"post_tokens":10328,"cumulative_dropped_tokens":122076,"duration_ms":61111,"preserved_segment":{"head_uuid":"aa403070-45d9-4367-9ef4-d13df13b945f","anchor_uuid":"05647663-22b6-4a24-841d-b8cd4b4a5e89","tail_uuid":"68257977-ad8e-45a9-a14d-af2d6233e799"},"preserved_messages":{"anchor_uuid":"05647663-22b6-4a24-841d-b8cd4b4a5e89","uuids":["aa403070-45d9-4367-9ef4-d13df13b945f","aa1d0fa9-e11f-41cc-b708-677b015244b3","44b0fdcd-2678-4b9f-834b-eed3465324d0","a75030a6-eab1-404e-a649-07f7854ffeb6","7cf8dcdc-196c-40b2-9e21-8905632424dc","68257977-ad8e-45a9-a14d-af2d6233e799"],"all_uuids":["aa403070-45d9-4367-9ef4-d13df13b945f","aa1d0fa9-e11f-41cc-b708-677b015244b3","44b0fdcd-2678-4b9f-834b-eed3465324d0","a75030a6-eab1-404e-a649-07f7854ffeb6","7cf8dcdc-196c-40b2-9e21-8905632424dc","68257977-ad8e-45a9-a14d-af2d6233e799"]}},"logical_parent_uuid":"68257977-ad8e-45a9-a14d-af2d6233e799","session_id":"e60805ed-c36d-4e22-8274-acc0a44d64d1"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n   The user's only message is the task text, verbatim:\n   \"You are implementing in this repo (read AGENTS.md first; follow it strictly: spec first, English only, negentropy, migrations numbered next (0065+), all writes via Database.write(), tx.now).\n   TASK: Add validated task drafts and safe batch publication. Operators must be able to assemble complete task definitions before workers can claim them, fixing immediate-claim and immutable-field races on create/edit/dependencies.\n   1. Inspect current create/edit/dependency lifecycle (apps/api/src/argus_api/tasks, mcp_server.py, docs/specs/task-edit, task-dependencies, worker-lifecycle, mcp-operations, existing batch tools such as any create_tasks). Update living specs FIRST (new docs/specs/task-drafts.spec.md in six-section template, link from docs/README.md, and amend task lifecycle + MCP operations specs): draft lifecycle, publication atomic vs partial semantics (explicit per-item outcomes; state clearly which mode each endpoint/tool offers), authorization, limits, version (expected_version/stale detection), idempotency keys and retry semantics.\n   2. Implement persisted drafts (new migration, upgrade-safe and idempotent) with explicit publish, through shared domain logic used by BOTH REST and MCP. No fake dependency, no fictitious capability, no placeholder ready tasks. Drafts are never claimable/eligible. Validation at publish: project, spec, acceptance, capability, real dependency graph (refs between drafts in the same batch map to the real new task IDs; cycles refused 422; existing deps exist), permissions, limits. Publish is safe vs concurrent claim: a task becomes visible/eligible only once complete, in one write transaction. Duplicate/retried publish with same idempotency key creates no duplicates and returns the same outcome. Editing a stale draft version is refused (409 stale_version). Existing create API stays backward compatible; do NOT add stricter policy that breaks legitimate non-coding tasks (e.g. don't require repository/coding fields in general). Out of scope: arbitrary cancellation, provider pins, deployment.\n   3. Tests (pytest in apps/api/tests): nothing eligible/claimable before publish; retries/idempotency; dependent IDs/edges correct; cycles; invalid payloads; concurrent publish vs claim (threads) cannot expose partial definitions; process restart (reopen DB, drafts persist); stale version edits; auth (worker denied, orchestrator/admin allowed); migration upgrade from previous schema + idempotence.\n   4. Run `make check` (or the equivalent uv ruff/ty/pytest commands if make is unavailable) and fix everything. Do not commit; leave changes in the working tree. Report what you ran and any skips honestly.\"\n\n   Rules from the persona and AGENTS.md:\n   - Finish with a message starting \"COMPLETE:\" plus a summary, or \"FAIL:\"/\"ASK:\". Keep messages concise.\n   - English only. Never commit secrets. Ruff and Biome are the formatting authority.\n   - Spec first; link every doc from docs/README.md.\n   - Never edit a shipped migration.\n   - No network calls inside a write transaction.\n   - Do not commit.\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n   - Python 3.12 uv workspace (apps/api, packages/core), FastAPI, aiosqlite with SQLite WAL and a single writer, pydantic v2. Linting is ruff (select E4,E7,E9,F,B,I,UP,SIM,RUF,ASYNC,C4,PIE,S,PERF; line length 88), type checking is ty, tests are pytest (asyncio_mode auto, `-n auto`).\n   - `Database.write()` yields a `Tx` with `conn`, `now`, `events`, and `savepoint()`. The savepoint context rolls back and drops recorded events on exception, then re-raises. Events are published after commit; any error rolls back the whole transaction.\n   - Errors in argus_api.errors: DomainError(message, code=, details=), plus NotFoundError 404, ConflictError 409, ForbiddenError 403 and ValidationFailedError 422.\n   - Versions are the `updated_at` ISO string from `ts()`. A strictly increasing version is `ts(max(tx.now, old + 1µs))`.\n   - `service.create_task(tx, body: TaskCreate, actor, *, as_worker=None, hourly_limit=None, untrusted=False)` does the following:\n     - applies kind defaults to fields not in `model_fields_set`;\n     - checks the project (`unknown_project`), `project_required`, pins, the harness account, and that dependencies exist;\n     - sets the state to READY if all deps succeeded, else PENDING, or AWAITING_APPROVAL with `requires_approval` or when over the hourly limit;\n     - inserts task_deps and records `task.created`.\n   - Migrations are applied via PRAGMA user_version; versions must have no gaps.\n   - MCP tools are `@tool(MANAGERS)` async functions that call `_call(ctx, \"METHOD\", \"/path\", json=..., params=...)`. MANAGERS = orchestrator + admin.\n   - Route hourly limit pattern: `limit = settings.max_tasks_per_agent_hour; hourly_limit = limit if caller.agent_id is not None and limit > 0 else None`.\n   - The `make check` target runs: lint (ruff check, ruff format --check, pnpm lint, `python3 scripts/validate_docs.py`), typecheck (ty, pnpm typecheck), test (pytest -n auto, pnpm test) and openapi-check. `make openapi` regenerates packages/api-client/openapi.json and schema.d.ts.\n\n3. Files and Code Sections:\n   - **Created: docs/specs/task-drafts.spec.md** (six sections plus a Verification boundary). Content:\n     - Drafts live in `task_drafts`; they are never in tasks, so they are never claimable or listed.\n     - The body is TaskCreate fields plus `depends_on_drafts`, with deps limited to 100 total. Saving is lenient about completeness.\n     - Version is `updated_at`. PATCH takes `{expected_version, changes}`: null resets a field, and a no-op writes nothing. DELETE takes `?expected_version=`.\n     - A published draft returns 409 `draft_published` on edit or discard. At most 200 open drafts are allowed (409 `too_many_drafts`).\n     - Publish is `POST /api/task-drafts/publish` with `{idempotency_key 1–200 chars, mode atomic|partial (default atomic), drafts:[{draft_id, expected_version}] 1–50}`. Both REST and MCP offer both modes.\n     - Publish validation covers: existence, open, version, valid TaskCreate, non-blank spec plus at least one non-blank acceptance criterion (drafts only), kind/project/pins/harness, capabilities declared by a pool or non-archived agent (`unknown_capability`), deps existing, depends_on_drafts in the batch or already published, cycles (`dependency_cycle` with path), and the hourly policy.\n     - Tasks are created in topological order through create_task.\n     - Atomic refusal precedence: 404 not_found > 409 stale_version > 409 draft_published > 422 dependency_cycle > 422 validation_failed. `details` entries take the form \"<draft_id>: <reason>\".\n     - In partial mode, outcomes are published/rejected/skipped.\n     - The answer is `{idempotency_key, mode, replayed, items:[{draft_id, outcome, task_id, state, code, errors}]}`.\n     - Idempotency: the answer is stored in `task_draft_publications`; a replay returns `replayed: true`; a different request with the same key gets 409 `idempotency_key_reused`; a refused atomic publish stores nothing.\n     - Publish vs claim is safe through the single writer and one transaction.\n     - Permissions are manager-only, reads included; 403 is decided first.\n     - It contains a table of REST endpoints and MCP tools (`create_task_draft`, `list_task_drafts`, `get_task_draft`, `edit_task_draft`, `discard_task_draft`, `publish_task_drafts`) and an errors table.\n   - **Edited specs** (via a python replace script):\n     - docs/README.md: added the Task drafts link after Task edit.\n     - worker-lifecycle.spec.md: a 3.2 bullet saying a draft is not a task; 3.6 orchestrator row now says \"draft and publish tasks ([task drafts](task-drafts.spec.md))\"; the 3.7 tool list now includes the six draft tools.\n     - task-edit.spec.md: a Non-Goals pointer to drafts.\n     - task-dependencies.spec.md: a 3.1 bullet on in-batch draft refs becoming edges.\n     - mcp-operations.spec.md: a coverage-audit table row for drafts.\n   - **Created: packages/core/src/argus_core/task_drafts.py**:\n     - Constants: MAX_OPEN_DRAFTS=200, MAX_PUBLISH_BATCH=50, MAX_DRAFT_DEPENDENCIES=100.\n     - `TaskDraftBody(TaskCreate)`: extra=\"forbid\", `title: str = Field(default=\"\", max_length=200)`, `depends_on_drafts: list[str] = []`, and a validator for the dependency count.\n     - `TaskDraft`: id, body, version, created_by/at, updated_by/at, published_at, published_task_id.\n     - `TaskDraftPage{items, total}`.\n     - `TaskDraftEdit{expected_version, changes: dict min_length=1}`.\n     - `PublishItem`.\n     - `PublishRequest`: idempotency_key, mode Literal default \"atomic\", drafts 1..50, and a validator that each draft is named once.\n     - `PublishOutcome{draft_id, outcome Literal[published,rejected,skipped], task_id, state, code, errors}`.\n     - `PublishResult{idempotency_key, mode, replayed=False, items}`.\n   - **Created: apps/api/src/argus_api/db/migrations/0065_task_drafts.sql**, which creates with IF NOT EXISTS:\n     - table `task_drafts` (STRICT): id PK, body JSON, created_by, created_at, updated_by, updated_at, published_at, published_task_id REFERENCES tasks(id), publication_key;\n     - partial index `task_drafts_open (created_at, id) WHERE published_at IS NULL`;\n     - table `task_draft_publications` (STRICT): idempotency_key PK, request_digest, answer JSON, actor, created_at.\n   - **Created: apps/api/src/argus_api/tasks/drafts.py** (the shared domain logic):\n     - Reads: `get_draft(conn, id)`, `list_drafts(conn)`.\n     - `create_draft(tx, body, actor)` checks the open count against MAX_OPEN_DRAFTS (409 too_many_drafts) and stores `_stored(body)`, a sorted-key JSON of `model_dump(mode=\"json\", exclude_unset=True)`. Only set fields are stored so kind defaults still apply.\n     - `edit_draft(tx, id, changes, expected_version, actor)`: `_open_row` checks draft_published and stale_version; it merges the patch, drops null keys, and validates TaskDraftBody (ValidationFailedError with details). A no-op returns the current draft; otherwise it writes a tick-incremented version.\n     - `discard_draft(tx, id, expected_version)`.\n     - `publish(tx, req, actor, *, hourly_limit=None)` runs in this order:\n       1. Check the stored key: a different digest gets 409 idempotency_key_reused; the same digest returns the stored answer with replayed=True.\n       2. Per-item checks: not_found, draft_published, stale_version.\n       3. Map outside published drafts to their task ids.\n       4. `_incomplete()` checks TaskCreate validation, spec/acceptance completeness, and depends_on_drafts not in the batch.\n       5. `_order()` does a Kahn topological sort plus `_cycle_from` DFS; cycle members are rejected with dependency_cycle.\n       6. Each remaining draft, in order, is skipped if any in-batch dep was not published. Otherwise it builds a TaskCreate with depends_on = existing + mapped ids, and inside `tx.savepoint()` it calls `service.create_task(...)`, runs `_check_capabilities` (SQL union of json_each over pools.capabilities and non-archived agents.capabilities), marks the draft published, and records event subject \"task_draft\" kind \"task_draft.published\" with {task_id, idempotency_key}. A DomainError makes the item rejected.\n       7. Atomic mode with failures raises `_atomic_refusal(failed)`, which picks the error class and code by precedence and rolls back the transaction. Otherwise it inserts the publication row and returns the result.\n     - Helpers: `_rejected`, `_digest` (sha256 of the mode plus [id, version] pairs), `_errors`, `_row`, `_rows`, `_open_row`, `_to_draft`.\n     - Possible lint concerns: one long line in `_atomic_refusal` (the `details` comprehension) and one in `_digest` exceed 88 chars, so they need ruff format. The `errors = []` variable typing may need `list[str]` for ty.\n   - **Created: apps/api/src/argus_api/tasks/draft_routes.py**: router prefix \"/task-drafts\", tag \"task-drafts\", all routes using ManagerDep:\n     - POST \"\" (201) create_draft;\n     - GET \"\" list;\n     - POST \"/publish\" (computes hourly_limit from SettingsDep);\n     - GET \"/{draft_id}\";\n     - PATCH \"/{draft_id}\" with a TaskDraftEdit body;\n     - DELETE \"/{draft_id}\" (204) with Query expected_version min_length=1.\n   - **Edited: apps/api/src/argus_api/main.py**: imports `task_drafts_router` from argus_api.tasks.draft_routes and adds it after tasks_router in the include loop.\n   - **Files read for reference:**\n     - apps/api/src/argus_api/tasks/service.py: create_task, edit_task, _check_dependencies, _path_back, check_create, _apply_kind_defaults, _resolve_harness_account, MAX_DEPENDENCIES=100.\n     - tasks/routes.py, deps.py, mcp_server.py: INSTRUCTIONS text, `_call`, the create_task/edit_task/set_task_dependencies tools, `audiences`, MANAGERS.\n     - tests: test_mcp.py, test_task_dependencies.py, conftest.py, test_migrate.py.\n     - db/database.py, migrate.py, errors.py, events.record.\n\n4. Errors and fixes:\n   - None yet; nothing has been run against the new code. No user feedback beyond the initial task.\n\n5. Problem Solving:\n   - Design: drafts sit in a separate table, so they are inherently unclaimable.\n   - Publish reuses `create_task` inside savepoints, avoiding duplicated validation rules.\n   - Partial mode uses savepoints; atomic mode raises at the end so the whole transaction rolls back.\n   - Idempotency relies on a stored answer plus a request digest.\n   - Separate `depends_on_drafts` avoids ambiguity between draft ids and task ids.\n   - Stricter rules (completeness, capability) apply only to draft publish, so direct create stays backward compatible.\n\n6. All user messages:\n   - Only the single task message quoted in full in section 1. Security constraint, verbatim: \"Never commit secrets (gitleaks runs in CI and pre-push)\" (from AGENTS.md). The user's instruction: \"Do not commit; leave changes in the working tree. Report what you ran and any skips honestly.\"\n\n7. Pending Tasks:\n   - Add the MCP tools to mcp_server.py, all `@tool(MANAGERS)` and forwarding to REST:\n     - `create_task_draft(ctx, draft: TaskDraftBody)` → POST /task-drafts with `draft.model_dump(mode=\"json\", exclude_unset=True)`;\n     - `list_task_drafts` → GET;\n     - `get_task_draft(draft_id)`;\n     - `edit_task_draft(draft_id, expected_version, changes: dict)` → PATCH;\n     - `discard_task_draft(draft_id, expected_version)` → DELETE with params;\n     - `publish_task_drafts(idempotency_key, drafts: list[PublishItem], mode=\"atomic\")` → POST /task-drafts/publish.\n   - Mention the draft tools in the INSTRUCTIONS text and in skills/argus-orchestrator/SKILL.md (apps/api/src/argus_api/skills/argus-orchestrator/SKILL.md). Backticked names must be real tools.\n   - Check whether any test pins the tool count or whether integrations/nanoclaw/README.md mirrors the instructions.\n   - Write apps/api/tests/test_task_drafts.py covering:\n     - nothing claimable before publish (`tasks.claim(tx, A, [])` returns None, and list_tasks is empty);\n     - idempotent replay and key reuse returning 409;\n     - in-batch dependency ids and edges, with dependent PENDING and root READY;\n     - cycles, including self-reference, returning 422;\n     - invalid payloads: incomplete spec/acceptance, unknown keys, unknown capability, missing dep;\n     - partial vs atomic outcomes and skipped items;\n     - concurrent publish vs claim using threads or concurrent tasks (claim never sees a dependent without its edges or a partial batch);\n     - reopening the DB with drafts persisted;\n     - stale version edit/discard returning 409 and published-draft edits returning 409;\n     - auth over REST and MCP: worker gets 403 and the tools are not listed; orchestrator and admin are allowed;\n     - migration upgrade from `migrations[:64]` with existing data, then reopen as a no-op, plus running the 0065 SQL twice for idempotence.\n     - Use `insert_agent` from api_support for capability agents. Check the agents table capabilities column used by insert_agent.\n   - Run `make openapi` to regenerate packages/api-client/openapi.json and schema.d.ts. This needs pnpm install; check /tmp/pnpm.log.\n   - Run `make check` (or `uv run ruff check .`, `uv run ruff format .`, `uv run ty check`, `uv run pytest -n auto`, `python3 scripts/validate_docs.py`, plus the pnpm targets) and fix all failures.\n   - Do not commit. Send a final \"COMPLETE:\" message listing the commands run and any skips.\n\n8. Current Work:\n   Just finished creating draft_routes.py and registering `task_drafts_router` in main.py (confirmed by grep: line 63 import, line 274 in the router tuple; `max_tasks_per_agent_hour: int = 100` exists in config.py). The next piece is the MCP tools.\n\n9. Optional Next Step:\n   - Add the six draft MCP tools to apps/api/src/argus_api/mcp_server.py, importing `TaskDraftBody` and `PublishItem` from argus_core.task_drafts. Update INSTRUCTIONS and the orchestrator SKILL.md.\n   - Then write apps/api/tests/test_task_drafts.py, run `make openapi`, and run `make check`, fixing everything. This follows the task's steps 2–4: \"Implement persisted drafts ... through shared domain logic used by BOTH REST and MCP\", then tests, then \"Run `make check` ... and fix everything. Do not commit.\"\n   - Send the user a brief progress update first (\"Routes done; adding MCP tools, then tests and make check\").\nContinue the conversation from where it left off without asking the user any further questions. Resume directly — do not acknowledge the summary, do not recap what was happening, do not preface with \"I'll continue\" or similar. Pick up the last task as if the break never happened.\n\nThe messages after this summary are the most recent messages from before compaction, kept verbatim. The summary was written without seeing them, so something it says has not happened yet may already have happened in them."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e60805ed-c36d-4e22-8274-acc0a44d64d1","uuid":"05647663-22b6-4a24-841d-b8cd4b4a5e89","timestamp":"2026-10-31T23:07:40.713Z","isSynthetic":true}
