{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01EwcUA2dBBqQ9K8iDNAFS4q","type":"tool_result","content":"11:from base64 import b64decode\n12:from collections.abc import AsyncGenerator, Callable\n13:from contextlib import asynccontextmanager\n14:from datetime import datetime\n15:from pathlib import Path\n16:from types import FunctionType\n17:from typing import Annotated, Any, Literal\n18:from urllib.parse import urlsplit\n20:import httpx2 as httpx\n21:from argus_core.auth import Scope\n22:from argus_core.continuation import (\n27:from argus_core.task_drafts import PublishItem, TaskDraftBody\n28:from argus_core.task_edit import TaskChanges\n29:from argus_core.tasks import ExecutorModel, HarnessModel\n30:from fastapi import FastAPI\n31:from mcp.server.context import CallNext, HandlerResult, ServerRequestContext\n32:from mcp.server.mcpserver import Context, MCPServer\n33:from mcp.server.mcpserver.exceptions import ToolError\n34:from mcp.server.mcpserver.resources import TextResource\n35:from mcp.server.transport_security import TransportSecuritySettings\n36:from mcp.shared.exceptions import MCPError\n37:from mcp.types import INVALID_REQUEST\n38:from pydantic import BaseModel, Field\n39:from starlette.types import ASGIApp, Receive, Send\n40:from starlette.types import Scope as AsgiScope\n42:from argus_api.auth import authenticate\n43:from argus_api.errors import UnauthorizedError\n65:assemble related tasks before any worker can claim them, create_task_draft each one\n66:(depends_on_drafts links drafts) and publish_task_drafts them together. Lists\n1217:async def create_task_draft(ctx: Context, draft: TaskDraftBody) -> dict:\n1219:    publish_task_drafts. `draft` takes create_task's fields (same rules) plus\n1271:async def publish_task_drafts(\n## Rules\n\nYou **must**:\n\n- Act only through the Argus MCP tools. If a tool you need is missing or\n  refuses you, say which tool and why, and stop. Never script REST, `curl`, SQL\n  or Docker around it.\n- Give every `answer_decision` / `answer_decisions` item a fresh `request_id`\n  (e.g. `<decision_id>-1`). A retry with the same id is replayed, not refused.\n- Pass the current `version` as `expected_version` on `edit_task`,\n  `set_task_dependencies` and `update_pool`. On `409 stale_version`, read the\n  object again, re-decide, then retry. Never blindly resend.\n- Read evidence before you accept anything (see \"Reviewing a result\").\n- Follow `next_cursor` while `has_more` is true. One page is not the whole set;\n  `total` is.\n- Read `unknown` as \"not known\", never as success or zero. This covers an\n  instance fact's `source`, a quota figure and a readiness check with `ok=null`.\n- Read the effect back after every write (`get_tasks`, `inspect_pool`), and\n  wait with `wait_for_events` instead of polling in a loop.\n\nYou **must not**:\n\n- Answer a decision whose `audience` is `human`. Only an admin can (you get a\n  403). Tell the human what waits and why, and move on.\n- Accept, approve or reject in bulk without reading each item. `answer_decisions`\n  takes one explicit answer per decision on purpose.","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e60805ed-c36d-4e22-8274-acc0a44d64d1","uuid":"5aaccb1b-5aac-4d5d-ba91-ccdc77558d68","timestamp":"2026-10-31T23:07:45.106Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"11:from base64 import b64decode\n12:from collections.abc import AsyncGenerator, Callable\n13:from contextlib import asynccontextmanager\n14:from datetime import datetime\n15:from pathlib import Path\n16:from types import FunctionType\n17:from typing import Annotated, Any, Literal\n18:from urllib.parse import urlsplit\n20:import httpx2 as httpx\n21:from argus_core.auth import Scope\n22:from argus_core.continuation import (\n27:from argus_core.task_drafts import PublishItem, TaskDraftBody\n28:from argus_core.task_edit import TaskChanges\n29:from argus_core.tasks import ExecutorModel, HarnessModel\n30:from fastapi import FastAPI\n31:from mcp.server.context import CallNext, HandlerResult, ServerRequestContext\n32:from mcp.server.mcpserver import Context, MCPServer\n33:from mcp.server.mcpserver.exceptions import ToolError\n34:from mcp.server.mcpserver.resources import TextResource\n35:from mcp.server.transport_security import TransportSecuritySettings\n36:from mcp.shared.exceptions import MCPError\n37:from mcp.types import INVALID_REQUEST\n38:from pydantic import BaseModel, Field\n39:from starlette.types import ASGIApp, Receive, Send\n40:from starlette.types import Scope as AsgiScope\n42:from argus_api.auth import authenticate\n43:from argus_api.errors import UnauthorizedError\n65:assemble related tasks before any worker can claim them, create_task_draft each one\n66:(depends_on_drafts links drafts) and publish_task_drafts them together. Lists\n1217:async def create_task_draft(ctx: Context, draft: TaskDraftBody) -> dict:\n1219:    publish_task_drafts. `draft` takes create_task's fields (same rules) plus\n1271:async def publish_task_drafts(\n## Rules\n\nYou **must**:\n\n- Act only through the Argus MCP tools. If a tool you need is missing or\n  refuses you, say which tool and why, and stop. Never script REST, `curl`, SQL\n  or Docker around it.\n- Give every `answer_decision` / `answer_decisions` item a fresh `request_id`\n  (e.g. `<decision_id>-1`). A retry with the same id is replayed, not refused.\n- Pass the current `version` as `expected_version` on `edit_task`,\n  `set_task_dependencies` and `update_pool`. On `409 stale_version`, read the\n  object again, re-decide, then retry. Never blindly resend.\n- Read evidence before you accept anything (see \"Reviewing a result\").\n- Follow `next_cursor` while `has_more` is true. One page is not the whole set;\n  `total` is.\n- Read `unknown` as \"not known\", never as success or zero. This covers an\n  instance fact's `source`, a quota figure and a readiness check with `ok=null`.\n- Read the effect back after every write (`get_tasks`, `inspect_pool`), and\n  wait with `wait_for_events` instead of polling in a loop.\n\nYou **must not**:\n\n- Answer a decision whose `audience` is `human`. Only an admin can (you get a\n  403). Tell the human what waits and why, and move on.\n- Accept, approve or reject in bulk without reading each item. `answer_decisions`\n  takes one explicit answer per decision on purpose.","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01EwcUA2dBBqQ9K8iDNAFS4q","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
